---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WriteInBlock from '../components/WriteInBlock.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { graph, profilePage, breadcrumb } from '../lib/schema';

const path = '/about';
const schema = graph([
  profilePage({
    name: `Meet ${site.candidate.name}`,
    description: `About ${site.candidate.name}, write-in candidate for ${site.candidate.office}.`,
    path,
  }),
  breadcrumb([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Meet Meghann', path },
  ]),
]);
---

<BaseLayout title="Meet Meghann" description={`About ${site.candidate.name}, write-in candidate for ${site.candidate.office}.`} schema={schema}>
  <section class="bg-navy text-white">
    <div class="container-narrow py-14 lg:py-20 text-center">
      <p class="text-xs font-heading font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-red mb-3">My story</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-display font-extrabold text-white">Meet {site.candidate.name}</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-white/70">Write-in candidate for {site.candidate.office}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="container-narrow py-14 lg:py-20 space-y-10 text-lg text-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Woodstock has been my home for nineteen years
        <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-red">[Meghann: confirm — nineteen per your announcement, or twenty?]</span>.
        It's where my husband Mike and I have made our life and are raising our two children. It's where
        I've built a business, served our schools, and spent every working day helping the people who walk
        through the doors of town government. My roots here are deep, and so is my faith in this community.
      </p>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-display font-extrabold text-navy mb-4">Service to the community</h2>
        <p>
          I served on the Onteora Board of Education, because I believe the people closest to a community
          should have a real voice in shaping it. Today I serve as Woodstock's First Deputy Town Clerk, where
          I've been entrusted with carrying out the full duties of the Town Clerk's office. Over the past ten
          months <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-red">[Meghann: confirm timeframe]</span>, I've had a
          front-row seat to how our town actually works: how departments collaborate, where things get stuck,
          and how much quiet, dedicated effort it takes to serve residents well.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-display font-extrabold text-navy mb-4">The professional background behind the candidate</h2>
        <p>
          Before and alongside my public service, I've spent more than twenty-five years
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-red">[Meghann: confirm]</span> in administration, human
          resources, business management, bookkeeping, and organization — across public health, retail, the
          restaurant industry, and the arts.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          I'm also the founder of a business that helps other businesses get organized: building budgets,
          setting up bookkeeping, and creating the kind of clear, sustainable systems that let an organization
          run smoothly instead of lurching from crisis to crisis. That's not a talking point — it's what I do
          for a living. And it's exactly the skill set a town needs in its Supervisor: someone who understands
          budgets, operations, and how to build systems that serve people reliably.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl lg:text-3xl font-display font-extrabold text-navy mb-4">Why heart matters</h2>
        <p>
          I believe the greatest responsibility any of us can accept is caring for a place that is caring for
          us. For me, that place is Woodstock. This is a town where community still matters — where neighbors
          show up for one another, where volunteers give more than anyone asks, and where public servants work
          every day because they care. I want to lead in a way that honors that.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 font-display font-bold text-navy">That's why I'm asking you to write me in.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <WriteInBlock tone="light" />
</BaseLayout>
